title: Places, asking, files and problems
card: Chapter 8 | Places | Where things are
say:
  Games and drawings need to know where things are. In Fathom, a place is a value too.
uncard

new: places.fathom
type:
  genesis:
    set home to 100 horizontal 50 vertical
    set step to 30 horizontal 40 vertical
    scrawl home plus step
    scrawl "The step is ", the size of step, " long."
    scrawl "It goes ", (home plus step) of horizontal, " across."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 2-6
spot: line 2
say:
  A hundred horizontal, fifty vertical, is a flat place: a hundred across, and fifty down. On a screen, down is more.
  A place can have a depth too, for three D.
spot: line 4
say: Places can be added and taken away, and made bigger or smaller with times.
spot: line 5
say: The size of a place is how far it is from zero. Thirty across and forty down is fifty long.
spot: line 6
say: And of horizontal is just the across part. Of vertical is the down part.
spot: off
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 8 | Birth and existence | Where a thing starts, and where it is now
say:
  Here's a special pair of words. Give a kind of thing a part called birth, and it gets a part called existence by itself.
  Birth is where it starts. Existence is where it is now.
uncard
clear
type:
  a ball has:
    birth (a flat place)
    radius (a number)
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    conjure a ball as red
    set the birth of red to 100 horizontal 50 vertical
    set the radius of red to 20
    set the existence of red to the existence of red plus 30 horizontal 40 vertical
    scrawl "Red began at ", the birth of red, " and is now at ", the existence of red
    conjure a ball as blue
    set the birth of blue to 160 horizontal 90 vertical
    set the radius of blue to 20
    if red touches blue: scrawl "They touch!"
    if the existence of red is within 50 of the existence of blue: scrawl "And they're close."
    set the existence of red to the birth of red
    scrawl "Red is home again at ", the existence of red
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 1-4
say: A ball has a birth, which is a flat place, and a radius.
zoom: lines 7-11
spot: line 8
say: Setting the birth of red puts its existence there too.
spot: line 10
say: Then we move it, by adding to its existence.
spot: off
zoom: lines 12-18
spot: line 15
say:
  Touches asks whether two things' circles overlap. Each needs a birth, which gives it an existence, and a radius.
spot: line 16
say: Is within fifty of asks whether two places are fifty or less apart. That's handy for picking things up in a game.
spot: line 17
say: And setting existence to birth sends it back to where it started.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 8 | Asking | Questions for the person using the program
say: A program can ask the person using it a question, and wait for the answer.
uncard
clear
type:
  genesis:
    ask "What's your name? " into name
    ask "How old are you? " into age (a number)
    scrawl "Hi ", name, "! In ten years you'll be ", age plus 10, "."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 2-4
spot: line 2
say: Ask shows the question, and keeps what the person types under a name, as text.
spot: line 3
say: With a number in brackets, it keeps asking until a number is typed.
spot: off
zoom: out
run: and keep going
say: When a program asks, the answer box at the bottom is where we type.
answer: Sam
answer: ten
zoom: output
say: Ten is a word, not a number, so it asks again.
wait
zoom: out
answer: 11
until finished
zoom: output
say: Hi Sam. In ten years you'll be twenty one.
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 8 | Files | Keeping things after the program ends
say: Programs can write files, and read them back.
uncard
line: 4
type:

    inscribe "Name: " plus name plus new line into file "visitors.txt"
    add "Age: " plus age to file "visitors.txt"
    for each line in lines of file "visitors.txt":
      scrawl "> ", line
zoom: lines 5-8
spot: line 5
say:
  Inscribe makes a file holding this text, or replaces it if it's already there. New line is a line break.
spot: line 6
say: Add to file adds a line to the end of a file.
spot: line 7
say:
  And lines of file reads a file back, as a list of lines. Contents of file gives the whole file as one piece of text.
spot: off
zoom: out
run: and keep going
answer: Sam
answer: 11
until finished
zoom: output
wait
zoom: out

card: Chapter 8 | When things go wrong | Try, the wound, and raising an error
say:
  Sometimes things go wrong while a program runs. A file might be missing. Let's see what happens.
uncard
clear
type:
  genesis:
    set crew to a list of ("Ann", "Bo")
    scrawl item 5 of crew
    scrawl "This line never runs."
  and the universe said i love you
run: expect a problem
zoom: output
say:
  The program stops, with the line, and the reason in plain words. There is no item five in a list of two items.
wait
zoom: out
say: To carry on instead, put the lines that might go wrong under try.
clear
type:
  to fly, given fuel (a number):
    if fuel falls below 10: raise an error with "not enough fuel (only " plus fuel plus ")"
    scrawl "Up we go!"
  and the universe said i love you

  genesis:
    try:
      scrawl contents of file "missing.txt"
    if that went wrong:
      scrawl "No luck: ", the wound
    try:
      fly with 3
    if that went wrong:
      scrawl "Grounded: ", the wound
    scrawl "Still going."
  and the universe said i love you
zoom: lines 7-10
spot: lines 7-8
say: Try, and below it, the lines that might go wrong.
spot: lines 9-10
say:
  If that went wrong, at the same indent, right after, says what to do instead. Inside it, the wound is the reason, as text.
spot: off
zoom: lines 1-4
spot: line 2
say:
  Your own commands can go wrong on purpose, with raise an error. Try catches that the same way.
spot: off
zoom: out
run
zoom: output
say: No luck reading the missing file. Grounded, with only three fuel. And the program is still going.
wait
zoom: out
